# The Recommended rule of the same name holds every other puff word.
# `genuinely` sits here, because it sometimes separates a real case
# from an apparent one (`a line is added only when the file genuinely
# ends in a blank line`). The adjective `genuine` stays out, since it
# usually means authentic (`the badge in the footer is genuine`).
#
# `enhance` and the sentence adverb `Additionally,` sit here for the
# same reason. Each also appears in plain human-written docs, and
# `Additionally,` hit 47 of them in the kubernetes and nix.dev docs.
# `enhanced` stays out, because it opens feature names (`Enhanced
# Networking`, `Security Enhanced Linux`). `additionally` counts only
# with a glued comma, since mid-sentence it modifies a verb (`the flag
# additionally checks the signature`).
expr main [genuinely, enhance, enhances, enhancing, (additionally,)]
let message "Puff. State the fact and let the reader judge its weight."
let description "Flags genuinely, enhance, and a sentence-opening additionally, which usually inflate a claim without informing."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The badge in the footer is genuine."
allows "The path is contended under load."
allows "The enhancement label marks feature requests."
allows "The flag additionally checks the signature."
